WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.700
Delegate Agent solves a practical command

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.399
line problem. You may want a

00:00:05.399 --> 00:00:08.099
child coding runtime to review a

00:00:08.099 --> 00:00:10.799
diff, investigate a failure, or implement

00:00:10.799 --> 00:00:13.498
a scoped change, but each runtime

00:00:13.498 --> 00:00:16.198
expects different flags, prompt delivery, safety

00:00:16.198 --> 00:00:18.898
controls, and output formats. This repository

00:00:18.898 --> 00:00:21.598
wraps those differences in one Python

00:00:21.598 --> 00:00:24.297
CLI. The same command surface can

00:00:24.297 --> 00:00:26.997
launch Cursor Agent, Factory Droid, OpenAI

00:00:26.997 --> 00:00:29.697
Codex, Claude Code, or Kimi Code,

00:00:29.697 --> 00:00:32.396
while keeping local records that parent

00:00:32.396 --> 00:00:35.096
agents can inspect later. The top-level

00:00:35.096 --> 00:00:37.796
path is deliberately small. bin/delegate.py imports

00:00:37.796 --> 00:00:40.495
src/delegate_agent/cli.py, and that module owns the

00:00:40.495 --> 00:00:43.195
main control flow. It parses arguments,

00:00:43.195 --> 00:00:45.895
resolves the workspace, loads configuration, builds

00:00:45.895 --> 00:00:48.594
a Request object, and decides whether

00:00:48.594 --> 00:00:51.294
the run is a dry run,

00:00:51.294 --> 00:00:53.994
a tracked launch, or a persistent

00:00:53.994 --> 00:00:56.693
worktree launch. Configuration is layered so

00:00:56.693 --> 00:00:59.393
local automation can be predictable without

00:00:59.393 --> 00:01:02.093
hiding operator settings. Embedded defaults come

00:01:02.093 --> 00:01:04.793
first. User config, workspace config, and

00:01:04.793 --> 00:01:07.492
DELEGATE_CONFIG overlay those defaults. The validator

00:01:07.492 --> 00:01:10.192
checks provider sections, policy, reasoning declarations,

00:01:10.192 --> 00:01:12.892
tracking, retention, isolation, and worktree settings

00:01:12.892 --> 00:01:15.591
before any child process starts. The

00:01:15.591 --> 00:01:18.291
first safety idea is mode. Safe

00:01:18.291 --> 00:01:20.991
mode is for review and investigation.

00:01:20.991 --> 00:01:23.690
Work mode is edit capable. This

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:26.390
boundary is separate from reasoning effort.

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:29.090
A higher reasoning effort can ask

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:31.789
a model to think more, but

00:01:31.789 --> 00:01:34.489
it does not change sandboxing, network

00:01:34.489 --> 00:01:37.189
access, approval mode, or edit permission.

00:01:37.189 --> 00:01:39.889
The second safety idea is isolation.

00:01:39.889 --> 00:01:42.588
Safe runs normally execute in a

00:01:42.588 --> 00:01:45.288
temporary detached worktree or a directory

00:01:45.288 --> 00:01:47.988
copy, so ordinary relative-path edits do

00:01:47.988 --> 00:01:50.687
not touch the source checkout. Work

00:01:50.687 --> 00:01:53.387
runs can stay in the source

00:01:53.387 --> 00:01:56.087
checkout, or they can create a

00:01:56.087 --> 00:01:58.786
preserved Git worktree and branch for

00:01:58.786 --> 00:02:01.486
later review. Each runtime gets a

00:02:01.486 --> 00:02:04.186
tailored harness. Cursor and Kimi still

00:02:04.186 --> 00:02:06.885
use argv prompt transport, so Delegate

00:02:06.885 --> 00:02:09.585
redacts prompt text in public argv

00:02:09.585 --> 00:02:12.285
and manifests. Droid uses a private

00:02:12.285 --> 00:02:14.984
prompt file. Codex and Claude receive

00:02:14.984 --> 00:02:17.684
prompts over stdin, which keeps task

00:02:17.684 --> 00:02:20.384
text out of process argv. When

00:02:20.384 --> 00:02:23.084
tracked execution begins, Delegate creates a

00:02:23.084 --> 00:02:25.783
local run record under dot delegate.

00:02:25.783 --> 00:02:28.483
The runner writes a manifest, mutable

00:02:28.483 --> 00:02:31.183
state, a bounded snapshot, stdout and

00:02:31.183 --> 00:02:33.882
stderr logs, stream events, and sometimes

00:02:33.882 --> 00:02:36.582
a completion report. These files are

00:02:36.582 --> 00:02:39.282
local runtime state, not source files

00:02:39.282 --> 00:02:41.981
to commit. Those records power the

00:02:41.981 --> 00:02:44.681
inspection commands. Runs lists recent or

00:02:44.681 --> 00:02:47.381
active runs. Snapshot shows current status,

00:02:47.381 --> 00:02:50.080
isolation details, recent events, and bounded

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:52.780
assistant text. Run output selects the

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:55.480
best parent facing result, then falls

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.180
back to recovered final text or

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:00.879
bounded log diagnostics. Persistent worktrees add

00:03:00.879 --> 00:03:03.579
a full lifecycle. Delegate checks that

00:03:03.579 --> 00:03:06.279
Git has a valid head, the

00:03:06.279 --> 00:03:08.978
source checkout is clean, pass through

00:03:08.978 --> 00:03:11.678
mode is off, and the child

00:03:11.678 --> 00:03:14.378
binary exists. It then creates a

00:03:14.378 --> 00:03:17.077
branch, launches the child in the

00:03:17.077 --> 00:03:19.777
worktree, records review commands, and later

00:03:19.777 --> 00:03:22.477
refuses unsafe cleanup unless the caller

00:03:22.477 --> 00:03:25.176
opts in. The codebase is intentionally

00:03:25.176 --> 00:03:27.876
lean. Runtime Python dependencies are zero.

00:03:27.876 --> 00:03:30.576
The current tracked snapshot is dominated

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:33.275
by Python, with about twenty nine

00:03:33.275 --> 00:03:35.975
thousand lines. Tests are larger than

00:03:35.975 --> 00:03:38.675
source, which matches the project’s focus

00:03:38.675 --> 00:03:41.375
on command contracts and safety boundaries.

00:03:41.375 --> 00:03:44.074
The main maintenance hotspot is src/delegate_agent/cli.py.

00:03:44.074 --> 00:03:46.774
It is the coordination center for

00:03:46.774 --> 00:03:49.474
parsing, request building, prompt framing, temporary

00:03:49.474 --> 00:03:52.173
isolation, and runtime dispatch. Worktree management

00:03:52.173 --> 00:03:54.873
is the next hotspot because cleanup,

00:03:54.873 --> 00:03:57.573
dirty state, merge checks, and registry

00:03:57.573 --> 00:04:00.272
drift all meet there. If you

00:04:00.272 --> 00:04:02.972
are contributing, choose the subsystem first.

00:04:02.972 --> 00:04:05.672
Runtime flag changes start in cli.py.

00:04:05.672 --> 00:04:08.371
Registry and output changes start in

00:04:08.371 --> 00:04:11.071
runner.py, run_registry.py, and run_output_commands.py. Persistent worktree

00:04:11.071 --> 00:04:13.771
changes start in isolation.py, worktree_execution.py, and

00:04:13.771 --> 00:04:16.470
worktree_mgmt.py. You can remember Delegate as

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:19.170
three layers. First, the CLI builds

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:21.870
a safe and explicit request. Next,

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:24.570
the runner records what the child

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:27.269
runtime does. Finally, inspection and worktree

00:04:27.269 --> 00:04:29.969
commands make the result usable without

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:32.219
guessing where the logs went.
